   480	def _is_contained_pinned(candidate: Path, canonical_domain: Path) -> bool:
   481	    """Containment check for a *pre-canonicalized, pinned* domain root (PR-3
   482	    §2.5) -- only `candidate` is canonicalized here; `canonical_domain` never
   483	    is.
   484	
   485	    This is deliberately a different function from `_is_contained`, not an
   486	    overload of it: `_is_contained` re-canonicalizes *both* sides on every
   487	    call, which is exactly right for the project root (a project directory
   488	    is not expected to be symlink-swapped mid-run) but is the wrong contract
   489	    for an external reference root. A reference root's canonical form is
   490	    computed once, at `load_reference_roots` time, specifically so that a
   491	    `~/wiki` symlink swapped out from under a long-running verification pass
   492	    cannot silently change what "inside the root" means partway through that
   493	    same run -- the root is canonicalized once and then *pinned* for the
   494	    rest of the run. Passing a non-canonical `canonical_domain` here would
   495	    silently defeat that pinning (each call would re-resolve it, following
   496	    whatever the symlink currently points at), so the entry assertion below
   497	    makes that misuse fail loudly instead of silently.
   498	    """
   499	    assert _canonical(canonical_domain) == canonical_domain, (
   500	        "_is_contained_pinned requires an already-canonical domain; pass "
   501	        "_canonical(root) once at load time, never the raw declared path"
