   581	    citation. Rule B has no project-declared base to resolve such a path
   582	    against, so — exactly like a `scheme://` URL — it is exempt rather than
   583	    checked (and rather than mis-resolved: `Path(base) / "/abs/x"` silently
   584	    discards `base` and re-checks the literal absolute path against the real
   585	    filesystem, which is not what this rule is verifying). See the module
   586	    docstring for the known-uncovered case this leaves (e.g. an external
   587	    `~/.llm-wiki/...` design-doc store) and for `citations_exempt_external`,
   588	    the coverage field that now counts how many spans this exemption
   589	    swallowed instead of doing so silently.
