   602	    Reviewers commonly cite a position *within* a file rather than just the
   603	    file itself: `plugins/foo/scripts/check_setup.py:123` (a line number),
   604	    `docs/x.md:10-20` (a line range), `.hopper/tasks/foo.md::root` (a named
   605	    anchor), or `app/kernel-client/swift/X.swift:44-46,443-507` (several
   606	    disjoint ranges in one citation — PR-1, external-citation-base-spec-
   607	    20260727.md §5: measured against the fair proxy corpus, this comma-
   608	    separated extension alone resolves 10 previously-dangling citations, 7
   609	    of them in the implementation-era subset — the same implementation-era
   610	    count the entire external-reference-base protocol surface would have
   611	    resolved, at a cost of 3 characters instead of ~500 LOC and a new trust
   612	    domain). The locator is not part of the path — checking the literal
   613	    locator-suffixed string against the filesystem always fails even when
   614	    the file plainly exists. The `::anchor` form is tried first since it is
   615	    the more specific shape (and would otherwise be partially consumed by
   616	    the line-number pattern if the anchor itself looked numeric). Returns
   617	    `cleaned` unchanged if neither suffix is present.
   618	    """
